- How a change reaches main: the git-gatekeeper (`scripts/git-gatekeeper.py check-in` — specification: `docs/cross-project/git-gatekeeper-design.md`) is the permanent path — one program, one credential, one door; agents never push to main. Until its credential work lands (activation waits on build slice 6), the gate is dormant and the interim lane applies: commit to the working branch, push it, and the user's Mac-side agent reviews and merges. In-flight work answers to `status <digest>` and `cancel <digest>`; `audit` checks main's live protection against the design.
